#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("The other things that you would need to do to avoid some of those issues that we see today.. is for example to.. Each of these things that we mentioned that people find problematic, there's ways to fix many of them For example, you find leaving the Prayer, committing Zina, and Weed, and these things, and listening to Music.. You find these things, they have one commonality. You know what that one commonality is? They have bad friends! People have bad friends, bad companions, bad surroundings, bad environments That's why all of you probably know the Hadith of the راهب (Rahib: Monk), Hadith of the Rahib who killed 99 Souls, you heard this Hadith right?", "very popular, famous Hadith and that Rahib what does he say? to the person.. The person of knowledge, he says to him: Leave the village, leave that bad place that you're in. Why? because your environment affects you, your surroundings affect you, your friends affect you Prophetﷺ said: لا تُصَاحِبْ إِلَّا مُؤْمِنًا Aaah, I want you to understand this Hadith: (Do not befriend except a Believer) Do not BEFRIEND except a Believer! So when you bring this Michael and you say it's my friend, No Habibi! (My dear) لا تُصَاحِبْ إِلَّا مُؤْمِنًا (Do not befriend except a Believer) He can be your colleague, a person you know, we're not saying be bad to them, be good to them and everything..", "of course there is بِرّ (Birr: Goodness). Allah commands you to be good to them. But he's not your friend! Friend is that who you tell your secrets, influences your behaviour, your understanding, you spend most of your time with,.. that's a friend. Can not be someone who is most of the time in the Club, in the Bar, listening to Music.. Where are you going to be? You are going to be in the Masjid, and in the club, in the bar with your friends? I don't know unless you know, how can time travel, or you're two personalities in one, that can not happen..", "Prophetﷺ said (do not befriend except a Believer), and he mentioned many Ahadith, that maybe some of you know, some of you don't know For example: المرءُ عَلَى دِينِ خَلِيلِهِ (You're upon the religion of your friend) If your friend is an Atheist, and you come tell me \"I'm a Muslim practising..\" Prophetﷺ said (you're upon the religion of your friend) فَلْيَنْظُرْ أَحَدُكمْ مَنْ يُخَالِل (Look who you're taking as a friend) And the Prophetﷺ says خليل (Khalil), يخالل (to befriend). You know what the word يخالل means in the Arabic language? Is when something seeps through something else, do you understand?", "Because these ideas and behaviours of your friends, they literally seep through you, and your ideas, and your beliefs. That's why you find them say \"you're the sum of the five people you hang out with\", they say this thing, all the time you hear them saying this example, because it's true, who you spend your time with, is going to influence you. Some people can come and say \"Now look life is difficult for us man, we live in the West, everyone is like Bars, Clubs, Women walking by..\" Is that an excuse? The Prophetﷺ did he have it more difficult or easier?", "Difficult or easier? With the Prophetﷺ..? His Companions.. Women were circulating the Kaaba completely naked They have brothels and houses of committing Zina and Shirk, and they were doing Usury and Interest, they were killing each other for the lamest things, Wars for tens of years for ridiculous reasons, killing left and right.. So, whatever you see today in the community, there is nothing.. They used to drink Alcohol more than water, you know the Hadith when Alcohol became forbidden, and they put it in the roads, roads were soaked! You imagine roads were soaked, even today probably.. Roads were soaked from the Alcohol, they used to drink it like water.", "So anything of what you see was there, so what made those people the Companions of the Prophetﷺ be firm on what they believe? It was their 'Aqeeda. It was them knowing what I told you a minute ago, knowing for a fact this is the Haqq from Allah. It is irrelevant what people around me are doing, it is irrelevant how many women there, they try.. Even they come to you themselves, it does not matter, it is irrelevant who listens to music -day and night- that's irrelevant. I know this is by Yaqeen, by Certainty, I know this is the Haqq, therefore I know I should behave based on that, I don't care how other people behave, they're not going to stand before Allah.", "I will stand before Allah So having friends is the most important thing. Friend. Having righteous friends The second thing I'm going to mention is the School. And the one thing I want to add to the righteous friends, we said what's the effect of a bad friend on you. But the good friend, what is the effect? Is the opposite effect: increasing you in knowledge, calling you to Prayer, reminding you of Allahﷻ, and on the Day of Judgement, the Hadith says: (people will say: Ô Allah, we're not happy with our friends not being with us in Jannah, but in the fire) –Muslims, yeah!", "would be punished in the fire– (and Allah would say go take your friends..) Shafa'a شفاعة (Intercession), good friends can take you and me from the Fire Just being around good people, good Companionship, can be a reason for you to be taken from the Fire and enter Jannah, instead of being punished in the fire. SubhanAllah, know the importance of having good friends",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |\"")

